{"parentUuid":"555d29f2-c0ec-4a24-8ab1-29cd2119f971","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg5VZFCHhBDHeiFYS8S2J","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The overlap is fixed, and the candle and bottle are replaced with an abstract object. The new build is live on the same link and QR you already have, so just refresh.\n\n**Overlap:** your screenshot showed the product card sitting on top of the Instagram caption card in the \"One input. Every deliverable.\" scene.\n- **Final view:** it's now two columns of cards with the photo in the gap between them, so they can't touch.\n- **Timing:** the photo settles in the middle first, and the cards appear afterwards.\n- **Short screens:** the photo is also capped by screen height, which was causing a second overlap with the caption on short laptops.\n- **Check:** I measured overlaps at 11 screen sizes (360 px phones to 1920×1080) across 7 scroll positions in the scene. It found none.\n- **Rerun:** the check is saved as `frontend/e2e/layout-overlap.mjs`, so you can run it again after any layout change.\n\n**Product:** a matte ceramic sphere on a plinth with a terracotta band. It has no illustrated label or face, so nothing looks cartoonish. It is used in the hero, the demo studio and the \"Try a sample product\" button.\n- **Sample listing:** the name is now \"Orb Desk Object\". The facts are matte ceramic sphere, 9 cm diameter, terracotta band on the base, and sold as a single piece.\n- **Sample status:** it's still labelled a sample, because it's a drawing and not a photo.\n\nI also re-ran the end-to-end app test (passes) and regenerated the screenshots and the demo video (now 79 s).\n\nNothing is committed yet. Say \"commit\" if you want it pushed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2311,"cache_read_input_tokens":650097,"output_tokens":548,"output_tokens_