{"parentUuid":"f39c3f38-7c4f-4901-b56a-cee9b2fa2214","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg5XGyT3KcuKT2hfRpkhW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've seen the recordings and the product photos. Now I'll check what HyperFrames actually is and whether it can be installed here."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6186,"cache_read_input_tokens":658119,"output_tokens":617,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":482},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6186,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":617,"cache_read_input_tokens":658119,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6186,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6186},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cg5XGxmcMeGaViK1agzPK","requestRef":"4222d4d8-d1e6-419b-a880-41788da5b94c","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3aebeffc-25c9-4362-8c0c-af382671db3d","timestamp":"2026-10-16T07:29:24.848Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"d1a90136-ab51-4450-87af-371f07f2f333","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/advikdivekar/Desktop/sellcraft","sessionId":"159a4645-4bae-4261-ac0b-464a7f4accd7","version":"2.1.300","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"3aebeffc-25c9-4362-8c0c-af382671db3d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg5XGyT3KcuKT2hfRpkhW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MFbspo5c19xoCQ1gCajw4b","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"HyperFrames HTML to video framework open source npm hyperframes render","mode":"standard"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6186,"cache_read_input_tokens":658119,"output_tokens":617,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":482},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6186,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":617,"cache_read_input_tokens":658119,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6186,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6186},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01MFbspo5c19xoCQ1gCajw4b":{"query":"HyperFrames HTML to video framework open source npm hyperframes render","mode":"standard"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cg5XGxmcMeGaViK1agzPK","requestRef":"4222d4d8-d1e6-419b-a880-41788da5b94c","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b8317df7-0398-4c14-aee8-6ba9e771d9da","timestamp":"2026-10-16T07:29:25.018Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"d1a90136-ab51-4450-87af-371f07f2f333","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/advikdivekar/Desktop/sellcraft","sessionId":"159a4645-4bae-4261-ac0b-464a7f4accd7","version":"2.1.300","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"159a4645-4bae-4261-ac0b-464a7f4accd7","hash":"08b10a5ca66aaa4cb9ea6300931d5e3a248cab1f18822bb7473215a320bd3941","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MFbspo5c19xoCQ1gCajw4b","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"HyperFrames HTML to video framework open source npm hyperframes render\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"gitee.com\",\"url\":\"https://gitee.com/taiyi-one/hyperframes\"},{\"title\":\"github.com\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/sparowjake-troll/hyperframes\"},{\"title\":\"github.com\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes\"},{\"title\":\"github.com\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/js0980420/hyperframes\"},{\"title\":\"gitee.com\",\"url\":\"https://gitee.com/mcnick/hyperframes\"},{\"title\":\"gitee.com\",\"url\":\"https://gitee.com/guangwenchen/hyperframes\"},{\"title\":\"gitee.com\",\"url\":\"https://gitee.com/yonja/hyperframes\"},{\"title\":\"heygen com hyperframes\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/iflow-mcp/heygen-com-hyperframes\"},{\"title\":\"HyperFrames: An Open-source Rendering Framework for Generating Video with HTML\",\"url\":\"https://silenceper.com/en/article/2026-05-02-hyperframes-html-video-rendering/\"}]\n\nHyperFrames is an open-source framework from HeyGen that renders HTML-based video to MP4, and the npm package is named `hyperframes`. The search results mostly agree on the basics, though several are unofficial mirrors.\n\n- **What it does:** The project turns HTML, CSS, media, and seekable animations into MP4 files, and its renderer seeks each frame in headless Chrome and encodes the result with FFmpeg, which makes output repeatable.\n- **Official source:** A third-party summary identifies HeyGen's open-source HTML video rendering framework, with the GitHub repo at heygen-com/hyperframes and docs at hyperframes.heygen.com. It lists Node.js >= 22, FFmpeg as requirements and Apache-2.0 as the license. That summary gives version 0.4.41, but the date of that figure isn't clear.\n- **Packages:** The monorepo includes @hyperframes/engine, a seekable page-to-video capture engine (Puppeteer + FFmpeg) and @hyperframes/producer, the full rendering pipeline (capture + encode + audio mix), plus a studio editor and a player web component.\n- **CLI and agents:** The README lists a dev-loop CLI covering init, lint, inspect, preview, render, and doctor. It is also designed for AI coding agents, installed via npx skills add heygen-com/hyperframes.\n\nCaveat: several search hits (gitee.com mirrors, and github.com forks under other accounts) are copies of the README rather than the official repo. Use heygen-com/hyperframes and the official docs for authoritative details. I did not verify the current npm version or the exact render command syntax.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]}}
