{"parentUuid":"016d14a4-2b0f-41e9-9ec8-4968de3375b8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e4bd6e61-219e-40d3-9a55-ced31e492eac","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01URsfKiE4vT4hdiVCDbx1q5","type":"tool_result","content":"# HyperFrames Quickstart\n\n## Requirements\n- Node.js 22+\n- FFmpeg\n\n## Install and create a project\n\n```bash\nnpx hyperframes init my-video\ncd my-video\n```\n\n## Preview\n\n```bash\nnpx hyperframes preview   # opens in the browser with live reload\n```\n\n## Render\n\n```bash\nnpx hyperframes render    # outputs MP4\n```\n\nThe README doesn't document render flags (output path, quality, fps). Check the CLI docs or the `/hyperframes-cli` skill for those.\n\n## Lint and inspect\n\nThe README doesn't show these commands. It only lists the CLI's capabilities, which include lint and inspect. Run `npx hyperframes --help` to see the exact syntax.\n\n## Optional: AI agent skills\n\nFor Claude Code, install the plugin:\n\n```bash\nclaude plugin marketplace add heygen-com/hyperframes\nclaude plugin install hyperframes@hyperframes\n```\n\nThen use `/hyperframes:hyperframes`. For standalone skills, run `npx skills add heygen-com/hyperframes`. Agents and non-interactive runs should use `npx hyperframes skills update`. Without `--skill`, a non-interactive `skills add` installs all 21 skills.\n\n## Composition format\n\nA composition is an HTML file. Timing and layering come from data attributes, and animation comes from a paused timeline registered on `window.__timelines`.\n\n```html\n<div id=\"stage\" data-composition-id=\"launch\" data-start=\"0\" data-width=\"1920\" data-height=\"1080\">\n  <video class=\"clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"6\" data-track-index=\"0\"\n         src=\"intro.mp4\" muted playsinline></video>\n\n  <h1 id=\"title\" class=\"clip\" data-start=\"1\" data-duration=\"4\" data-track-index=\"1\">Launch day</h1>\n\n  <audio data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"6\" data-track-index=\"2\"\n         data-volume=\"0.5\" src=\"music.wav\"></audio>\n\n  <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n  <script>\n    const tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n    tl.from(\"#title\", { opacity: 0, y: 40, duration: 0.8 }, 1);\n    window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n    window.__timelines.launch = tl;\n  </script>\n</div>\n```\n\n### Attributes\n- **Root:** `data-composition-id`, `data-start`, `data-width`, `data-height`. Resolution comes from width and height. The README doesn't show an fps or total-duration attribute.\n- **Clips (video, image, text):** `class=\"clip\"`, `data-start`, `data-duration`, `data-track-index`, and `src` for media.\n- **Audio:** the same timing attributes, plus `data-volume`.\n- **Animation:** use GSAP, CSS, Lottie, Three.js, Anime.js, WAAPI, or a custom adapter. Build GSAP timelines with `paused: true` and register them on `window.__timelines`.\n\n## Adding ready-made blocks\n\n```bash\nnpx hyperframes add data-chart\n```\n\nBrowse the catalog at hyperframes.heygen.com/catalog.\n\n## Gotchas\n- **Node.js 22+ and FFmpeg** are required. The README doesn't mention a separate Chrome download, but rendering uses headless Chrome through Puppeteer.\n- **Git LFS:** only needed if you clone the full repo for development. It stores about 240 MB of golden test `.mp4` files. To skip them:\n  ```bash\n  GIT_LFS_SKIP_SMUDGE=1 git clone https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes.git\n  ```\n- **Determinism:** the renderer seeks each frame, so animations must be seekable. Wall-clock animations need care."}]},"uuid":"1a5d6b03-37ce-4877-8d55-3f9120247696","timestamp":"2026-10-16T07:38:55.071Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":500908,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# HyperFrames Quickstart\n\n## Requirements\n- Node.js 22+\n- FFmpeg\n\n## Install and create a project\n\n```bash\nnpx hyperframes init my-video\ncd my-video\n```\n\n## Preview\n\n```bash\nnpx hyperframes preview   # opens in the browser with live reload\n```\n\n## Render\n\n```bash\nnpx hyperframes render    # outputs MP4\n```\n\nThe README doesn't document render flags (output path, quality, fps). Check the CLI docs or the `/hyperframes-cli` skill for those.\n\n## Lint and inspect\n\nThe README doesn't show these commands. It only lists the CLI's capabilities, which include lint and inspect. Run `npx hyperframes --help` to see the exact syntax.\n\n## Optional: AI agent skills\n\nFor Claude Code, install the plugin:\n\n```bash\nclaude plugin marketplace add heygen-com/hyperframes\nclaude plugin install hyperframes@hyperframes\n```\n\nThen use `/hyperframes:hyperframes`. For standalone skills, run `npx skills add heygen-com/hyperframes`. Agents and non-interactive runs should use `npx hyperframes skills update`. Without `--skill`, a non-interactive `skills add` installs all 21 skills.\n\n## Composition format\n\nA composition is an HTML file. Timing and layering come from data attributes, and animation comes from a paused timeline registered on `window.__timelines`.\n\n```html\n<div id=\"stage\" data-composition-id=\"launch\" data-start=\"0\" data-width=\"1920\" data-height=\"1080\">\n  <video class=\"clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"6\" data-track-index=\"0\"\n         src=\"intro.mp4\" muted playsinline></video>\n\n  <h1 id=\"title\" class=\"clip\" data-start=\"1\" data-duration=\"4\" data-track-index=\"1\">Launch day</h1>\n\n  <audio data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"6\" data-track-index=\"2\"\n         data-volume=\"0.5\" src=\"music.wav\"></audio>\n\n  <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n  <script>\n    const tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n    tl.from(\"#title\", { opacity: 0, y: 40, duration: 0.8 }, 1);\n    window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n    window.__timelines.launch = tl;\n  </script>\n</div>\n```\n\n### Attributes\n- **Root:** `data-composition-id`, `data-start`, `data-width`, `data-height`. Resolution comes from width and height. The README doesn't show an fps or total-duration attribute.\n- **Clips (video, image, text):** `class=\"clip\"`, `data-start`, `data-duration`, `data-track-index`, and `src` for media.\n- **Audio:** the same timing attributes, plus `data-volume`.\n- **Animation:** use GSAP, CSS, Lottie, Three.js, Anime.js, WAAPI, or a custom adapter. Build GSAP timelines with `paused: true` and register them on `window.__timelines`.\n\n## Adding ready-made blocks\n\n```bash\nnpx hyperframes add data-chart\n```\n\nBrowse the catalog at hyperframes.heygen.com/catalog.\n\n## Gotchas\n- **Node.js 22+ and FFmpeg** are required. The README doesn't mention a separate Chrome download, but rendering uses headless Chrome through Puppeteer.\n- **Git LFS:** only needed if you clone the full repo for development. It stores about 240 MB of golden test `.mp4` files. To skip them:\n  ```bash\n  GIT_LFS_SKIP_SMUDGE=1 git clone https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes.git\n  ```\n- **Determinism:** the renderer seeks each frame, so animations must be seekable. Wall-clock animations need care.","durationMs":12038,"url":"https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"016d14a4-2b0f-41e9-9ec8-4968de3375b8","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_temporary"},"session_id":"d1a90136-ab51-4450-87af-371f07f2f333","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/advikdivekar/Desktop/sellcraft","sessionId":"159a4645-4bae-4261-ac0b-464a7f4accd7","version":"2.1.300","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
