{"parentUuid":"ccdab645-c8cd-4b70-8d41-33362223c356","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e4bd6e61-219e-40d3-9a55-ced31e492eac","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MS3PT5okRTW4tiXDEnUjtC","type":"tool_result","content":"• connections page\nPASS\nno overlaps found\n--- big/new files to be committed:\n?? docs/brand/\n?? docs/demo/\n?? frontend/components/landing/scene.tsx\n?? frontend/components/logo.tsx\n?? frontend/e2e/layout-overlap.mjs\n?? frontend/public/mochi-mark.png\n?? frontend/public/mochi-tile.png\n?? frontend/public/sample-product-cutout.svg\n2052\tdocs/demo/mochi-demo-mobile.mp4\n1540\tdocs/brand/mochi-logo.png\n1108\tdocs/images/landing-hero-desktop.png\n892\tdocs/images/landing-hero-mobile.png\n--- secret scan of files to commit\nREADME.md:73:`scripts/dev-phone.sh` generates a random access code, requires it on every API call, and puts it in the QR link (`...trycloudflare.com/#k=CODE`). Without it, anyone who learned the tunnel URL could use your GPU or publish to your connected store. Locally (no tunnel) there is no code unless you set `ACCESS_CODE` in `backend/.env`.\nREADME.md:99:It starts the backend, the frontend and a Cloudflare quick tunnel, then prints an `https://…trycloudflare.com` URL and a QR code. Scan it with the iPhone camera. HTTPS gives Safari the secure context it needs for camera capture, clipboard and share, and the tunnel works even when the Wi-Fi blocks device-to-device traffic (or on cellular). Code changes hot-reload. Anyone with the link can use the app while it runs; stop with Ctrl+C.\n(none above = clean)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ad1b2528-688e-4b54-bb09-0950c201cbb2","timestamp":"2026-10-16T07:40:36.332Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"• connections page\nPASS\nno overlaps found\n--- big/new files to be committed:\n?? docs/brand/\n?? docs/demo/\n?? frontend/components/landing/scene.tsx\n?? frontend/components/logo.tsx\n?? frontend/e2e/layout-overlap.mjs\n?? frontend/public/mochi-mark.png\n?? frontend/public/mochi-tile.png\n?? frontend/public/sample-product-cutout.svg\n2052\tdocs/demo/mochi-demo-mobile.mp4\n1540\tdocs/brand/mochi-logo.png\n1108\tdocs/images/landing-hero-desktop.png\n892\tdocs/images/landing-hero-mobile.png\n--- secret scan of files to commit\nREADME.md:73:`scripts/dev-phone.sh` generates a random access code, requires it on every API call, and puts it in the QR link (`...trycloudflare.com/#k=CODE`). Without it, anyone who learned the tunnel URL could use your GPU or publish to your connected store. Locally (no tunnel) there is no code unless you set `ACCESS_CODE` in `backend/.env`.\nREADME.md:99:It starts the backend, the frontend and a Cloudflare quick tunnel, then prints an `https://…trycloudflare.com` URL and a QR code. Scan it with the iPhone camera. HTTPS gives Safari the secure context it needs for camera capture, clipboard and share, and the tunnel works even when the Wi-Fi blocks device-to-device traffic (or on cellular). Code changes hot-reload. Anyone with the link can use the app while it runs; stop with Ctrl+C.\n(none above = clean)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ccdab645-c8cd-4b70-8d41-33362223c356","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"rule"},"session_id":"d1a90136-ab51-4450-87af-371f07f2f333","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/advikdivekar/Desktop/sellcraft","sessionId":"159a4645-4bae-4261-ac0b-464a7f4accd7","version":"2.1.300","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
